Attendees (2): Shreyas (me), Maya Chen (Staff engineer)
Description: Weekly one-on-one.
</meeting>

<template>
1:1. Two people catching up regularly. Capture what each person raised, feedback in both directions and agreed follow-ups. Keep the tone personal and candid, and do not editorialise about anyone's performance.
Sections, in order:
1. Check-in: Two or three sentences on how each person is doing (workload, energy, morale), only as far as they shared it. Write one or two paragraph blocks of prose.
2. Topics: Each topic either person raised, with the key points and where it landed. Write bullet blocks, one idea each.
3. Feedback: Feedback given in either direction, attributed, in the giver's own words where possible. Omit the section if none was given. Write bullet blocks, one idea each.
4. Growth: Goals, skills, opportunities or concerns about career growth. Omit the section if not discussed. Write bullet blocks, one idea each.
5. Action items: Follow-ups for either person, with the owner and due date when stated. Write todo blocks, one action each, naming the owner and the due date when known.
</template>

